{"id":"mahabharata-7-166","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":166,"title":"षट्षष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 166 · Ashvatthaman learns of his father's death","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra laments that Drona, a brahmin, was killed by unrighteous means. Sanjaya tells how Ashvatthaman, hearing of his father's death, flies into rage and vows to destroy the Pandavas, calling on the Narayana weapon.","kn":"ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ದ್ರೋಣ ಅಧರ್ಮದಿಂದ ಹತನಾದನೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ದುಃಖಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಂದೆಯ ಸಾವು ಕೇಳಿ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಕೆರಳಿ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಶಪಥ ಮಾಡಿ ನಾರಾಯಣಾಸ್ತ್ರವನ್ನು ಆಹ್ವಾನಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र शोक करते हैं कि ब्राह्मण द्रोण अधर्म से मारे गए। संजय बताते हैं कि पिता की मृत्यु सुनकर अश्वत्थामा क्रोध में आकर पाण्डवों के नाश की प्रतिज्ञा करता है और नारायणास्त्र का आह्वान करता है।","te":"బ్రాహ్మణుడైన ద్రోణుడు అధర్మంగా హతుడయ్యాడని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు విలపిస్తాడు. తండ్రి మరణం విని అశ్వత్థామ ఆగ్రహించి పాండవులను నాశనం చేస్తానని ప్రతిజ్ఞ చేసి నారాయణాస్త్రాన్ని ఆహ్వానిస్తాడని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"அந்தணர் த்ரோணர் அதர்மமாகக் கொல்லப்பட்டதாகத் த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் புலம்புகிறான். தந்தையின் மரணத்தைக் கேட்ட அஸ்வத்தாமன் சினந்து பாண்டவரை அழிப்பதாகச் சபதம் செய்து நாராயணாஸ்திரத்தை அழைப்பதைச் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"ബ്രാഹ്മണനായ ദ്രോണർ അധർമമാർഗത്തിൽ കൊല്ലപ്പെട്ടല്ലോ എന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ വിലപിക്കുന്നു. പിതാവിന്റെ മരണവാർത്ത കേട്ട് കോപം പൂണ്ട അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് പാണ്ഡവരെ നശിപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് പ്രതിജ്ഞയെടുത്ത് നാരായണാസ്ത്രം വിളിക്കുന്നത് സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.166; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"नारायणास्त्रमोक्षपर्व","titleEn":"Narayanastramoksha Parva (Release of the Narayana weapon)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अधर्मेण हतं श्रुत्वा धृष्टद्युम्नेन संजय ।\nब्राह्मणं पितरं वृद्धमश्वत्थामा किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, when Ashvatthaman heard that the aged brahmin, his father, had been killed by Dhrishtadyumna through unrighteous means, what did he say?"}},{"n":2,"text":"मानुषं वारुणाग्नेयं ब्राह्ममस्त्रं च वीर्यवान् ।\nऐन्द्रं नारायणं चैव यस्मिन्नित्यं प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That mighty man held in himself the human weapons, those of Varuna and Agni, the Brahma weapon, and those of Indra and Narayana, all ever established in him."}},{"n":3,"text":"तमधर्मेण धर्मिष्ठं धृष्टद्युम्नेन संजय ।\nश्रुत्वा निहतमाचार्यमश्वत्थामा किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, that most righteous teacher was struck down unrighteously by Dhrishtadyumna; hearing of it, what did Ashvatthaman say?"}},{"n":4,"text":"येन रामादवाप्येह धनुर्वेदं महात्मना ।\nप्रोक्तान्यस्त्राणि दिव्यानि पुत्राय गुरुकाङ्क्षिणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great soul had learned the science of the bow from Rama, and had taught the divine weapons to his son, who longed for his father's teaching."}},{"n":5,"text":"एकमेव हि लोकेऽस्मिन्नात्मनो गुणवत्तरम् ।\nइच्छन्ति पुत्रं पुरुषा लोके नान्यं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this world men wish for one thing only that is better than themselves, a worthy son, and for nothing else at all."}},{"n":6,"text":"आचार्याणां भवन्त्येव रहस्यानि महात्मनाम् ।\nतानि पुत्राय वा दद्युः शिष्यायानुगताय वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great teachers hold secret teachings, and these they give either to a son or to a devoted pupil."}},{"n":7,"text":"स शिल्पं प्राप्य तत्सर्वं सविशेषं च संजय ।\nशूरः शारद्वतीपुत्रः संख्ये द्रोणादनन्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, Drona's son, the son of Sharadvat's daughter, mastered all that skill and more, and in battle stood next after Drona."}},{"n":8,"text":"रामस्यानुमतः शास्त्रे पुरंदरसमो युधि ।\nकार्तवीर्यसमो वीर्ये बृहस्पतिसमो मतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Rama's approval in the science of weapons, he was like Indra in battle, like Kartavirya in might, and like Brihaspati in intellect."}},{"n":9,"text":"महीधरसमो धृत्या तेजसाग्निसमो युवा ।\nसमुद्र इव गाम्भीर्ये क्रोधे सर्पविषोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a young man he was steady like a mountain, blazing like fire, deep like the ocean, and in anger like a serpent's venom."}},{"n":10,"text":"स रथी प्रथमो लोके दृढधन्वा जितक्लमः ।\nशीघ्रोऽनिल इवाक्रन्दे चरन्क्रुद्ध इवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the foremost charioteer in the world, a firm bowman who never tired, swift as the wind in battle, and moving like Death himself when angry."}},{"n":11,"text":"अस्यता येन संग्रामे धरण्यभिनिपीडिता ।\nयो न व्यथति संग्रामे वीरः सत्यपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was crushed by his arrows in battle; that hero of true prowess never wavers in a fight."}},{"n":12,"text":"वेदस्नातो व्रतस्नातो धनुर्वेदे च पारगः ।\nमहोदधिरिवाक्षोभ्यो रामो दाशरथिर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Versed in the Vedas and in vows, a master of archery, he was unshakable like a great ocean, as Rama, son of Dasharatha, once was."}},{"n":13,"text":"तमधर्मेण धर्मिष्ठं धृष्टद्युम्नेन संयुगे ।\nश्रुत्वा निहतमाचार्यमश्वत्थामा किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That most righteous teacher was killed in battle by Dhrishtadyumna through unrighteous means; hearing this, what did Ashvatthaman say?"}},{"n":14,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्य यो मृत्युः सृष्टस्तेन महात्मना ।\nयथा द्रोणस्य पाञ्चाल्यो यज्ञसेनसुतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, son of Yajnasena, was born of the Panchala king to be Drona's death, and so was his death made by that great-souled one."}},{"n":15,"text":"तं नृशंसेन पापेन क्रूरेणात्यल्पदर्शिना ।\nश्रुत्वा निहतमाचार्यमश्वत्थामा किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That cruel, wicked, short-sighted man killed the teacher; hearing this, what did Ashvatthaman say?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"छद्मना निहतं श्रुत्वा पितरं पापकर्मणा ।\nबाष्पेणापूर्यत द्रौणी रोषेण च नरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that his father had been killed by a sinner through trickery, Drona's son was filled with tears and with rage, O best of men."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्य क्रुद्धस्य राजेन्द्र वपुर्दिव्यमदृश्यत ।\nअन्तकस्येव भूतानि जिहीर्षोः कालपर्यये ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king of kings, as he grew angry a divine form appeared in him, like Death wishing to take creatures at the turn of the age."}},{"n":18,"text":"अश्रुपूर्णे ततो नेत्रे अपमृज्य पुनः पुनः ।\nउवाच कोपान्निःश्वस्य दुर्योधनमिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wiping his tear-filled eyes again and again, he sighed in anger and spoke these words to Duryodhana."}},{"n":19,"text":"पिता मम यथा क्षुद्रैर्न्यस्तशस्त्रो निपातितः ।\nधर्मध्वजवता पापं कृतं तद्विदितं मम ।\nअनार्यं सुनृशंसस्य धर्मपुत्रस्य मे श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know the sin done to my father, how base men struck him down when he had laid down his weapons, and I have heard of the ignoble cruelty of the son of Dharma, who carries the banner of righteousness."}},{"n":20,"text":"युद्धेष्वपि प्रवृत्तानां ध्रुवौ जयपराजयौ ।\nद्वयमेतद्भवेद्राजन्वधस्तत्र प्रशस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who enter battle, victory and defeat are certain, and one or the other must come; in that case death is praised."}},{"n":21,"text":"न्यायवृत्तो वधो यस्तु संग्रामे युध्यतो भवेत् ।\nन स दुःखाय भवति तथा दृष्टो हि स द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A death in battle that comes by lawful means to one who fights does not cause grief, and so that brahmin was seen to fall."}},{"n":22,"text":"गतः स वीरलोकाय पिता मम न संशयः ।\nन शोच्यः पुरुषव्याघ्रस्तथा स निधनं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father has surely gone to the world of heroes; that tiger among men met his end so, and should not be mourned."}},{"n":23,"text":"यत्तु धर्मप्रवृत्तः सन्केशग्रहणमाप्तवान् ।\nपश्यतां सर्वसैन्यानां तन्मे मर्माणि कृन्तति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But that he, acting righteously, had his hair seized in front of the whole army, this cuts into my vital parts."}},{"n":24,"text":"कामात्क्रोधादवज्ञानाद्दर्पाद्बाल्येन वा पुनः ।\nवैधर्मिकानि कुर्वन्ति तथा परिभवेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"People do unlawful deeds out of desire, anger, contempt, pride, or childishness, and also out of insolence."}},{"n":25,"text":"तदिदं पार्षतेनेह महदाधर्मिकं कृतम् ।\nअवज्ञाय च मां नूनं नृशंसेन दुरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great unrighteous act was done here by the son of Prishata, surely holding me in contempt, that cruel and wicked-souled man."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्यानुबन्धं स द्रष्टा धृष्टद्युम्नः सुदारुणम् ।\nअनार्यं परमं कृत्वा मिथ्यावादी च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna will see its terrible consequence, and so will the Pandava who spoke a lie, having done a most ignoble deed."}},{"n":27,"text":"यो ह्यसौ छद्मनाचार्यं शस्त्रं संन्यासयत्तदा ।\nतस्याद्य धर्मराजस्य भूमिः पास्यति शोणितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of righteousness who by trickery made the teacher lay down his weapon, today the earth will drink that man's blood."}},{"n":28,"text":"सर्वोपायैर्यतिष्यामि पाञ्चालानामहं वधे ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नं च समरे हन्ताहं पापकारिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By every means I will strive for the slaughter of the Panchalas, and I will kill the evildoer Dhrishtadyumna in battle."}},{"n":29,"text":"कर्मणा येन तेनेह मृदुना दारुणेन वा ।\nपाञ्चालानां वधं कृत्वा शान्तिं लब्धास्मि कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"By whatever deed, gentle or fierce, once I have slaughtered the Panchalas, O Kaurava, I shall find peace."}},{"n":30,"text":"यदर्थं पुरुषव्याघ्र पुत्रमिच्छन्ति मानवाः ।\nप्रेत्य चेह च संप्राप्तं त्राणाय महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O tiger among men, men want a son so that he may protect them from great fear, both here and in the next world."}},{"n":31,"text":"पित्रा तु मम सावस्था प्राप्ता निर्बन्धुना यथा ।\nमयि शैलप्रतीकाशे पुत्रे शिष्ये च जीवति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father reached the state of one without kin, though I, mountain-like, his son and pupil, was alive."}},{"n":32,"text":"धिङ्ममास्त्राणि दिव्यानि धिग्बाहू धिक्पराक्रमम् ।\nयन्मां द्रोणः सुतं प्राप्य केशग्रहणमाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shame on my divine weapons, shame on my arms, shame on my prowess, that Drona, having me for a son, had his hair seized."}},{"n":33,"text":"स तथाहं करिष्यामि यथा भरतसत्तम ।\nपरलोकगतस्यापि गमिष्याम्यनृणः पितुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall act so, best of the Bharatas, that even though my father has gone to the other world I shall be free of my debt to him."}},{"n":34,"text":"आर्येण तु न वक्तव्या कदाचित्स्तुतिरात्मनः ।\nपितुर्वधममृष्यंस्तु वक्ष्याम्यद्येह पौरुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A noble man should never praise himself, but unable to bear my father's killing, I shall speak of my manliness today."}},{"n":35,"text":"अद्य पश्यन्तु मे वीर्यं पाण्डवाः सजनार्दनाः ।\nमृद्नतः सर्वसैन्यानि युगान्तमिव कुर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today let the Pandavas with Janardana see my strength as I crush all their armies, as if bringing on the end of an age."}},{"n":36,"text":"न हि देवा न गन्धर्वा नासुरा न च राक्षसाः ।\nअद्य शक्ता रणे जेतुं रथस्थं मां नरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither gods nor gandharvas, nor asuras nor rakshasas, bull among men, can defeat me in battle today as I stand in my chariot."}},{"n":37,"text":"मदन्यो नास्ति लोकेऽस्मिन्नर्जुनाद्वास्त्रवित्तमः ।\nअहं हि ज्वलतां मध्ये मयूखानामिवांशुमान् ।\nप्रयोक्ता देवसृष्टानामस्त्राणां पृतनागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one in this world knows weapons better than Arjuna, except me. Among blazing ones I am like the sun among its rays, a user of the weapons made by the gods, standing in the army."}},{"n":38,"text":"कृशाश्वतनया ह्यद्य मत्प्रयुक्ता महामृधे ।\nदर्शयन्तोऽऽत्मनो वीर्यं प्रमथिष्यन्ति पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, loosed by me in the great battle, the sons of Krishashva will show their power and crush the Pandavas."}},{"n":39,"text":"अद्य सर्वा दिशो राजन्धाराभिरिव संकुलाः ।\nआवृताः पत्रिभिस्तीक्ष्णैर्द्रष्टारो मामकैरिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, O king, all directions will seem choked with streams of rain, covered with my sharp arrows, and people will see it."}},{"n":40,"text":"किरन्हि शरजालानि सर्वतो भैरवस्वरम् ।\nशत्रून्निपातयिष्यामि महावात इव द्रुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Scattering nets of arrows on every side with a dreadful sound, I will fell my enemies as a great storm fells trees."}},{"n":41,"text":"न च जानाति बीभत्सुस्तदस्त्रं न जनार्दनः ।\nन भीमसेनो न यमौ न च राजा युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu does not know that weapon, nor does Janardana, nor Bhimasena, nor the twins, nor King Yudhishthira."}},{"n":42,"text":"न पार्षतो दुरात्मासौ न शिखण्डी न सात्यकिः ।\nयदिदं मयि कौरव्य सकल्यं सनिवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor does the wicked son of Prishata, nor Shikhandi, nor Satyaki know this weapon that I hold, O Kaurava, with its release and its recall."}},{"n":43,"text":"नारायणाय मे पित्रा प्रणम्य विधिपूर्वकम् ।\nउपहारः पुरा दत्तो ब्रह्मरूप उपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago my father bowed to Narayana in due form and offered him a gift when he appeared in the form of a brahmin."}},{"n":44,"text":"तं स्वयं प्रतिगृह्याथ भगवान्स वरं ददौ ।\nवव्रे पिता मे परममस्त्रं नारायणं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Lord himself accepted it and granted a boon; my father chose as the supreme weapon the Narayana weapon."}},{"n":45,"text":"अथैनमब्रवीद्राजन्भगवान्देवसत्तमः ।\nभविता त्वत्समो नान्यः कश्चिद्युधि नरः क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, the Lord, best of gods, said to him: No other man will ever be your equal in battle."}},{"n":46,"text":"न त्विदं सहसा ब्रह्मन्प्रयोक्तव्यं कथंचन ।\nन ह्येतदस्त्रमन्यत्र वधाच्छत्रोर्निवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, brahmin, this weapon must never be hurled rashly, for it does not turn back until the enemy is slain."}},{"n":47,"text":"न चैतच्छक्यते ज्ञातुं को न वध्येदिति प्रभो ।\nअवध्यमपि हन्याद्धि तस्मान्नैतत्प्रयोजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor can it be known, lord, whom it should not kill; it may strike even one who is not to be slain, so it should not be used."}},{"n":48,"text":"वधः संख्ये द्रवश्चैव शस्त्राणां च विसर्जनम् ।\nप्रयाचनं च शत्रूणां गमनं शरणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killing in battle, fleeing, throwing down weapons, begging the enemy, and going for refuge, these are the means of calming the great weapon, O scorcher of foes."}},{"n":49,"text":"एते प्रशमने योगा महास्त्रस्य परंतप ।\nसर्वथा पीडितो हि स्यादवध्यान्पीडयन्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In every way it will torment one who, using it in battle, harasses those who should not be slain."}},{"n":50,"text":"तज्जग्राह पिता मह्यमब्रवीच्चैव स प्रभुः ।\nत्वं वर्षिष्यसि दिव्यानि शस्त्रवर्षाण्यनेकशः ।\nअनेनास्त्रेण संग्रामे तेजसा च ज्वलिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father took it, and the Lord said to him: You will rain many divine showers of weapons, and with this weapon you will blaze in battle with brilliance."}},{"n":51,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा स भगवान्दिवमाचक्रमे प्रभुः ।\nएतन्नारायणादस्त्रं तत्प्राप्तं मम बन्धुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this the Lord went up to heaven. That Narayana weapon was obtained by my kinsman, my father."}},{"n":52,"text":"तेनाहं पाण्डवांश्चैव पाञ्चालान्मत्स्यकेकयान् ।\nविद्रावयिष्यामि रणे शचीपतिरिवासुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With it I shall drive off the Pandavas, Panchalas, Matsyas and Kekayas in battle, as the husband of Shachi drove off the asuras."}},{"n":53,"text":"यथा यथाहमिच्छेयं तथा भूत्वा शरा मम ।\nनिपतेयुः सपत्नेषु विक्रमत्स्वपि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As I wish, so my arrows will become and fall on my foes, even as they strive bravely, O Bharata."}},{"n":54,"text":"यथेष्टमश्मवर्षेण प्रवर्षिष्ये रणे स्थितः ।\nअयोमुखैश्च विहगैर्द्रावयिष्ये महारथान् ।\nपरश्वधांश्च विविधान्प्रसक्ष्येऽहमसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing in battle I shall rain stones as I please, and with iron-headed birds of arrows I shall scatter great chariot-warriors, and without doubt I shall hurl many kinds of axes."}},{"n":55,"text":"सोऽहं नारायणास्त्रेण महता शत्रुतापन ।\nशत्रून्विध्वंसयिष्यामि कदर्थीकृत्य पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O scorcher of foes, with the great Narayana weapon I shall destroy my enemies and make the Pandavas contemptible."}},{"n":56,"text":"मित्रब्रह्मगुरुद्वेषी जाल्मकः सुविगर्हितः ।\nपाञ्चालापसदश्चाद्य न मे जीवन्विमोक्ष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hater of his friend, of brahmins, and of his teacher, that despicable wretch, that vile Panchala, will not escape me alive today."}},{"n":57,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा द्रोणपुत्रस्य पर्यवर्तत वाहिनी ।\nततः सर्वे महाशङ्खान्दध्मुः पुरुषसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this from Drona's son, the army turned back, and then all those best of men blew great conches."}},{"n":58,"text":"भेरीश्चाभ्यहनन्हृष्टा डिण्डिमांश्च सहस्रशः ।\nतथा ननाद वसुधा खुरनेमिप्रपीडिता ।\nस शब्दस्तुमुलः खं द्यां पृथिवीं च व्यनादयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joyfully they beat thousands of drums and kettledrums, and the earth, pressed by hooves and wheel-rims, resounded. That tumultuous sound filled the sky, heaven and earth."}},{"n":59,"text":"तं शब्दं पाण्डवाः श्रुत्वा पर्जन्यनिनदोपमम् ।\nसमेत्य रथिनां श्रेष्ठाः सहिताः संन्यमन्त्रयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that sound like the roar of a thundercloud, the Pandavas, best of charioteers, gathered together and took counsel."}},{"n":60,"text":"तथोक्त्वा द्रोणपुत्रोऽपि तदोपस्पृश्य भारत ।\nप्रादुश्चकार तद्दिव्यमस्त्रं नारायणं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, Drona's son, O Bharata, touched water and then brought forth that divine Narayana weapon."}}]}]}